# =============================================================================
# .env.example — ioe-grade2
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to `.env.local` for local use:  cp .env.example .env.local
# NEVER commit real values. `.env` and `.env*.local` are gitignored.
#
# NOTE: This app is a fully STATIC site (Next.js output: "export"). It has no
# backend, no database, and currently reads NO environment variables at runtime.
# The variables below are for the DEPLOY pipeline and for future client config.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare Pages deploy credentials (CI ONLY)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used by .github/workflows/deploy.yml. In production these live as GitHub
# Actions secrets (Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions), NOT in a file.
# Listed here only so you know what the deploy needs.

# API token for `wrangler pages deploy`. Create a CUSTOM token at
# Cloudflare > My Profile > API Tokens > Create Token > Create Custom Token.
#
# Policy (least privilege — grant ONLY this):
#   Scope:  Entire Account  (select your account, NOT "all accounts")
#     Pages: Write   <- required; lets the token deploy the build
#     Pages: Read    <- comes with it; lets the token list deployments
#   (Cloudflare may label these "Edit/Read" instead of "Write/Read" — same thing.)
#
#   Do NOT add DNS / Apps / Client-side security / all-zones scopes — not needed
#   to deploy a static site, and over-scoping is a leak risk.
#   Add "Zone > DNS > Edit" (scoped to ONE zone) only if this token also manages
#   a custom domain's DNS records.
#
#   Token expiration: set an expiry (e.g. 90 days) and rotate.
#   Client IP filtering: leave empty (GitHub Actions runners use dynamic IPs).
#
# In production this value lives as a GitHub Actions secret, NOT in this file.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# Your Cloudflare account ID (dashboard right sidebar).
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Future client-side config (optional, currently unused)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only variables prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ are exposed to the browser.
# Because the site is static, these are inlined at BUILD time, not at runtime —
# so they are PUBLIC. Never put a secret in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable.

# Example: analytics or a public site URL, if you add them later.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://ioe-grade2.pages.dev
